00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.210
episode

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.210
"On the Night

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.210
of Their Passionate Vows''

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.390
Oh, Lady Oscar.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:44.190
Dr. Lanson.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.350
I'm sorry, I know it's late,
but I'd like you to examine me.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.230
I've come prepared, Doctor.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.770
Please tell me truthfully.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.820
I wish to know what exactly
is happening to me.

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:04.600
You seem to have a stubborn cold, but it's
nothing you should be worried about.

00:03:05.110 --> 00:03:07.540
I coughed up blood several times.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:11.350
I know I have a sickness of the lungs.

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:15.610
What I wish to know is how
long do I have to live?

00:03:16.750 --> 00:03:19.450
Consumption isn't an incurable illness.

00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:25.200
I've known many patients who have been cured naturally
by living in a quiet environment with clean air.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.600
Doctor, I don't want to die either.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:31.690
But if that day is going to come, I'd like
to live my life to the fullest until then.

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:35.230
Freely... and following my heart...

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:39.490
My family has served the Jarjayes family
for generations as physicians.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.330
I can clearly remember the time you had a fever when
you were 3 years old, as if it were yesterday.

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:52.730
That is why I must say this to you.

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:57.900
Leave the military and move
to a quiet estate immediately.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.540
You mustn't think about anything,
or do any work.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:04.870
Just diligently bathe yourself in sunlight
and wait for God's mercy.

00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:09.060
At this rate, you'll only live 6 months at most.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:15.120
Thank you, Dr. Lanson.

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.020
I appreciate it.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:19.820
Ah, Lady Oscar.

00:04:20.520 --> 00:04:23.490
Um, how is André's condition?

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.870
I've been worried because
he hasn't visited lately.

00:04:27.230 --> 00:04:28.300
André?

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.580
André's condition?

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.250
Your servant, André hasn't told you yet?!

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:35.840
What do you mean?!

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:36.710
Please tell me!

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:43.380
<i>It's only a matter of time before
André Grandier becomes blind.</i>

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:45.100
André...

00:04:55.660 --> 00:05:00.230
<i>Blacksmiths had begun forging pikes
instead of forging horseshoes.</i>

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:06.410
<i>Bakers sold rusty weapons in their
storefronts instead of kneading dough.</i>

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:12.540
<i>Small groups, which gathered in street corners,</i>

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:16.500
<i>swelled to massive crowds in the square.</i>

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.470
Hip, hip, hurrah!

00:05:19.910 --> 00:05:23.010
Hip, hip, hurrah!

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:25.930
Hip, hip, hurrah!

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:32.270
Lady Oscar, what time will
you be returning tonight?

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:33.760
I'm not sure.

00:05:33.760 --> 00:05:36.230
I might stay overnight at the barracks.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:40.190
In that case, we should send a
messenger to Armand, the painter.

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:46.470
It was agreed that he would come
finish up the portrait this afternoon.

00:05:46.470 --> 00:05:48.160
Right, I remember now.

00:05:48.640 --> 00:05:49.810
Very well.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.450
In that case, I'll come back as soon as I can.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:52.620
Have him wait for me.

00:06:05.730 --> 00:06:10.850
Hey, I heard Company A was ordered to equip
for battle and was dispatched today.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:12.440
Yeah, I heard that, too.

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:15.800
Then maybe Company B will
be dispatched soon, too?

00:06:15.800 --> 00:06:18.140
Equip for battle against who though?

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.510
Who do you think?

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:21.580
Against the armed citizens.

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:24.400
I want nothing to do with that.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:25.950
We don't have a choice.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.340
This is what we're being paid for.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:28.650
Good point.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.820
Don't worry.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:32.550
I doubt our Company will be dispatched.

00:06:32.550 --> 00:06:34.180
I sure hope so.

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:55.260
It's awfully quiet today.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:07:00.440
Yes. It's because all the men from Company A
have been dispatched to Paris in full gear.

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:03.810
Paris has been in an uproar since this morning.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.080
Even the women and children have armed
themselves with brooms and sticks,

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.380
and are loudly protesting in every square.

00:07:08.920 --> 00:07:10.400
Have there been any casualties?

00:07:10.780 --> 00:07:12.490
No, it hasn't reached that point yet.

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.370
After all, they have 100,000 soldiers
glaring at them menacingly.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.300
Even if they're encouraged to take up arms,

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.870
all they have are old guns
and hastily made pikes at best.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:23.330
They haven't launched an attack
on the military, at least for now.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.600
I'm sure Company A was only
dispatched as a precaution.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:31.340
So if the situation worsens, Company B
will be dispatched, as well?

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.220
Yes, I believe so.

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:36.610
For that very reason, the Regiment
Command Center has sent word,

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.080
that Company B should stop patrolling
Paris starting today.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:41.080
I see. We're to be on standby then.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:41.740
Yes!

00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:43.260
Thank you.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:44.150
Please excuse me!

00:07:48.760 --> 00:07:49.490
Commander.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:53.950
You look pale and seem quite worn.

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:57.500
If you'd like, please go back to your
manor and be on standby there.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:59.660
If something should arise,
I'll send a messenger.

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:01.900
What are you talking about?

00:08:01.900 --> 00:08:03.120
I'm perfectly fine.

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:05.540
My wife passed away last year.

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.040
It was a sickness of the lungs.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:09.340
That is why I can tell!

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.380
I noticed it awhile back.

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.800
Please, do as I say...

00:08:21.120 --> 00:08:22.480
Colonel d'Agout.

00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.250
Thank you.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.980
I'll follow your suggestion.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.440
Hey, Alain, what is it?

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:43.080
The Commander wants to see you.

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:44.440
Oscar does?

00:08:47.480 --> 00:08:49.630
André Grandier, coming in!

00:08:50.390 --> 00:08:51.780
Did you call for me, Commander?

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:56.590
The situation in Paris is worsening.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:59.560
It's as though the people's voices could
be heard all the way to our barracks.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.550
How's that?

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:03.890
Oscar?

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.390
Oscar?

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:13.000
What the... Why did she call me,
if she's not going to be here?

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:19.880
<i>André...</i>

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:23.380
<i>You're no longer able to see, even me?</i>

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:31.920
André!

00:09:34.030 --> 00:09:35.380
Are you coming from my office?

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.950
I'm sorry, something came up
and I had to leave my office.

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:41.300
Oh, it's all right.

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:45.410
We're off-duty and are on standby today.

00:09:45.410 --> 00:09:46.840
Let's go back to the manor together.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.900
But if we're on standby, I should
stay here with the others.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.250
I want you to accompany me...

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:55.150
It's been a while...

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.220
Plus, going back alone isn't
as safe as it used to be.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:12.590
<i>By the afternoon, the crowds swelled even
larger and several groups began to move.</i>

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:17.410
The waves of the people are roaring
thunderously for freedom.

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.540
No one can stop us now.

00:10:19.540 --> 00:10:23.380
Waves can even alter the shape
of a boulder on the shore.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:26.110
Freedom, equality and benevolence...

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:28.120
See our flag flutter!

00:10:28.120 --> 00:10:30.490
Seine! Do not forget this day!

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:33.580
And the great billowing wave that
is about to reshape history!

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:39.030
<i>Taking advantage of the lightly guarded areas,</i>

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.790
<i>the crowds broke through and rushed in.</i>

00:10:43.130 --> 00:10:48.380
<i>First, they raided a food merchant's warehouse
along the Seine to relieve their hunger.</i>

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.380
<i>Afterwards, in search of guns,</i>

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:55.410
<i>the people fanned out across Paris, and targeted the
mansions and warehouses owned by weapon merchants.</i>

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.180
Could you open your eyes please?

00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:11.060
I'm sorry.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:16.030
It won't be much longer.

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:20.060
Once I finish painting your sapphire eyes,

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.170
everything will be finished.

00:11:34.250 --> 00:11:36.170
Done.

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:53.440
Done.

00:11:59.840 --> 00:12:02.070
Oh, this is...

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:06.820
She's dressed as Mars,
the God of War from the myths.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:08.520
You are indeed correct.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.790
On the surface, she's as tranquil as water,

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:15.090
but there's a fire burning inside her,
as though she's heading to the battlefield.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.340
That is what I saw in her.

00:12:17.690 --> 00:12:23.330
If it doesn't suit you, I'd like to take
it home and keep it as my treasure.

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:24.970
No, that won't be necessary.

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:26.270
It's magnificent!

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:28.970
It's as though there's another Oscar before us.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:33.440
It's been years since I've poured every last
ounce of my energy into a piece like this.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.240
André, what's the matter?

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.280
Come here and have a closer look.

00:12:37.280 --> 00:12:38.540
Yeah, in a moment...

00:13:04.270 --> 00:13:06.900
It's beautiful... beyond compare...

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:12.710
Your brilliant smile... It as though all the
light in this world is gathering upon you.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:18.110
The laurel wreath placed on your
blonde hair is especially brilliant.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:26.710
<i>André, there's no need to force yourself.</i>

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:29.290
<i>I already know you're blind.</i>

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:33.100
<i>I'm not wearing a laurel wreath in that portrait.</i>

00:13:38.480 --> 00:13:42.590
One... two... No, it's a field of white roses.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.280
I wonder which forest this is?

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.510
I know!

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.970
It's near the spring of Arras
where we visited once.

00:13:51.580 --> 00:13:53.170
Right, Oscar?

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:55.780
That's right, André.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:14:00.110
Armand said he went all the way
to Arras to make a sketch.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:02.120
It's a magnificent painting.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:06.760
Your grace, dignity and even
your joy are all expressed.

00:14:06.760 --> 00:14:11.990
I'll never forget your beauty in
\hthis painting. I'll never forget it...

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.000
Thank you, André.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:23.630
Thank you...

00:14:41.660 --> 00:14:42.660
Commander!

00:14:42.660 --> 00:14:44.910
I've come to relay a report on
the orders of Colonel d'Agout.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.570
Alain, you came all this way to—

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:53.540
I hereby report that we've received an order
from the Regiment Command Center!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.930
Tomorrow morning at 8AM,
the French Guards Company B...

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:00.010
...will advance to Paris' Tuileries Square,
fully equipped for battle!

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:04.960
Cooperate with the other regiments and
suppress the armed rioters, are the orders!

00:15:10.730 --> 00:15:11.930
So they've finally given the order.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:14.640
I'm afraid they have.

00:15:16.260 --> 00:15:17.230
Good work.

00:15:17.230 --> 00:15:20.060
Return to the barracks. I'll return shortly.

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:34.450
The saddles are ready.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:35.740
We can leave anytime.

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:39.620
Ah, Master.

00:15:39.620 --> 00:15:40.750
Please excuse me.

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:41.960
André.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.590
Yes.

00:15:42.590 --> 00:15:44.890
I hear you're going to battle tomorrow.

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:45.490
Yes.

00:15:45.490 --> 00:15:49.490
It could be tomorrow or the day after,
but eventually I'll be going to battle, as well.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:54.440
There's always a chance that
this may be the last time we meet.

00:15:54.440 --> 00:15:55.240
Yes.

00:15:55.240 --> 00:15:58.300
There's one thing I must tell you.

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:04.950
If you had been a noble, I would have
allowed you to marry Oscar for certain.

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:07.950
No, in fact, I would have given you
my wholehearted blessings.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:14.770
Do not die, André.

00:16:14.770 --> 00:16:16.120
Promise me you'll come back!

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:19.620
Of course, Master!

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:44.030
Let's go to the Invalides!

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:45.790
To the Invalides! To the Invalides!

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:46.980
To the Invalides! To the Invalides!

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.160
The Invalides?

00:16:52.160 --> 00:16:54.910
Makes sense, arms and ammunitions
are stored in that building.

00:17:06.010 --> 00:17:07.940
Royal Army soldiers!

00:17:07.940 --> 00:17:09.240
Get their weapons!

00:17:12.350 --> 00:17:14.130
André, stay close to me!

00:17:21.680 --> 00:17:23.060
Don't let them get away!

00:17:34.140 --> 00:17:34.830
André!

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:38.660
André!

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:40.740
André!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:56.630
We have very limited weapons and ammunition
compared to the royal army!

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:02.600
However, if the military opens fire and tries
to suppress us by force, we will fight!

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:08.560
After all, we have the backing of
96% of the people of France!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.020
That's right!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.100
Also,

00:18:11.100 --> 00:18:15.940
in each of our hearts, is the fiery courage
and rage that will deflect any bullet!

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.400
That's right!

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.550
Up ahead is dangerous, too.
Let's take another route.

00:18:29.960 --> 00:18:32.500
How's your head injury, André?

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:35.430
I'm fine. It's nothing serious.

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:39.380
How dare you deceive me all this time.

00:18:40.840 --> 00:18:42.170
About your right eye.

00:18:42.170 --> 00:18:43.910
Dr. Lanson told me everything.

00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.670
You're almost blind, aren't you?

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:53.500
Let's go back to the manor.

00:18:54.120 --> 00:18:57.620
I can't allow you to go to Paris tomorrow.

00:18:57.620 --> 00:19:00.780
You'll stay with Nanna and I'll go
back to the barracks alone.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:05.630
Please do as I say, André.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:07.620
I can't let anything happen to you.

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:15.600
I'm going with you, Oscar.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:22.610
I always have and I always will.

00:19:22.610 --> 00:19:24.220
I'll always be by your side.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:30.050
André... I used to be in love with Fersen.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:34.080
Despite knowing you loved me,
I still loved Fersen.

00:19:34.820 --> 00:19:38.540
Could you still really love someone like me?

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:42.490
I love everything about you.
For as long as I live...

00:19:48.670 --> 00:19:50.830
André, André...

00:19:51.440 --> 00:19:54.960
I love you, too... with all my heart.

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:02.680
I already knew that.

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.550
I've known it for years.

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:07.210
No, I knew it even before I was born...

00:20:26.640 --> 00:20:28.340
<i>André Grandier...</i>

00:20:28.340 --> 00:20:31.180
<i>I can live as long I have you.</i>

00:20:31.180 --> 00:20:33.040
<i>No, I want to live...!</i>

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:59.160
<i>It was the moment Oscar became
André Grandier's wife.</i>

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.560
<i>Oscar, I forgot to say goodbye to you.</i>

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:24.420
<i>No, perhaps it wasn't necessary,
since you're coming back.</i>

00:21:26.760 --> 00:21:28.350
Live, Oscar!

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.390
As your heart commands!

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.100
Um, Master...

00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:41.110
Our Lady had asked me to give this to you.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:44.250
Would you please read it for me?

00:21:45.020 --> 00:21:45.990
Yes.

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.590
What's the matter? Read it.

00:21:50.590 --> 00:21:53.490
Well... it's only one sentence.

00:21:53.490 --> 00:21:54.260
One sentence?

00:21:54.260 --> 00:22:00.250
''Thank you for all the love and devotion you
have bestowed on a daughter like me.''

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.360
What are you saying, Oscar?

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:06.220
You sound as though you're
truly saying goodbye.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:10.580
I won't allow it!

00:22:10.580 --> 00:22:12.010
I won't allow it, Oscar!

